course: dictionary
lesson: 8469
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as 1), 2) and 3). Salsa is one word that does this. The words around it give you clues about which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «Salsa grew up in New York and the Caribbean from Cuban and Puerto Rican music.» Here salsa is linked with music and with Cuba and Puerto Rico, so it means the lively dance and music. If the sentence were about food, such as «She dipped her chips in salsa», it would mean the sauce.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in another meaning. Does «sauce» fit «from Cuban and Puerto Rican music»? No. Does «dance» fit «dipped her chips in»? No. This checking is how you know you have picked the right meaning.
fact: Salsa means a spicy sauce, made from chopped tomatoes, onions, chillies and herbs.
fact: Salsa is also a lively dance and a kind of music from Latin America and the Caribbean, especially Cuba and Puerto Rico.
fact: In Spanish and Italian, «salsa» simply means sauce.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word, and the context tells you which meaning is wanted.
fact: In cooking lessons, tomato salsa is an easy no-cook recipe that practises knife safety and measuring.
exercise: «We scooped up the tomato salsa with tortilla chips.» What is salsa here? | A tomato plant | A lively partner dance | A cold drink | *A spicy sauce
exercise: «In PE we learned a salsa step and then spun round.» What does salsa mean here? | *A lively partner dance | A spicy sauce for dipping | A bowl of chips | A quiet song
exercise: «Our salsa class was full of spinning and laughter.» Which word shows that salsa is a dance and not a sauce? | laughter | full | *class | salsa
test: «Salsa grew up in New York and the Caribbean from Cuban and Puerto Rican music.» Which meaning fits best? | A spicy sauce | A kind of bread | *A lively dance and music from Latin America and the Caribbean | A loud shout
test: In Spanish, «salsa» means what? | A dance | A class | *Sauce | A chilli
exam: Ella reads «Mum put salsa on the table next to the chips.» Which meaning is right, and why? | A dance, because people dance at tables | *A sauce, because a table and chips go with food | A type of shoe, because it is on the table | A music festival, because the table is loud
